# 10. SALARY STRUCTURE

Create salary structures.

Example:

```text
Software Engineer

Basic              ₹40,000
HRA                ₹20,000
Special Allowance  ₹10,000
Transport           ₹5,000
---------------------------
Gross               ₹75,000
```

Employer contribution:

```text
Employer PF
Employer ESI
Other contribution
```

---

# 11. CTC

Support:

```text
Monthly CTC
Annual CTC
Gross Salary
Net Salary
Employer Contributions
```

Example:

```text
Annual CTC
= Gross Salary
+ Employer Contributions
+ Other Benefits
```

Do not assume CTC always equals gross salary.

---

# 12. EMPLOYEE SALARY ASSIGNMENT

Employees should be assigned salary structures.

Store:

```text
employee_id
salary_structure_id
effective_from
effective_to
version
status
```

Salary changes must preserve history.

Do not overwrite old salary information.

---

# 13. SALARY VERSIONING

Example:

```text
Jan-Jun:
₹60,000

Jul-Dec:
₹70,000
```

Payroll must calculate using the salary applicable during that payroll period.

---

# 14. RETROACTIVE SALARY CHANGE

Prepare architecture for:

```text
Salary effective from previous date
```

Example:

```text
Current date:
September

Salary revision:
Effective July
```

The system should identify whether payroll needs recalculation or arrears.

If arrears are not fully implemented in this phase, create a clean extension point.

---

# 15. PAYROLL PERIOD

Create payroll periods.

Example:

```text
September 2026
```

Fields:

```text
id
tenant_id
name
start_date
end_date
pay_date
status
```

Statuses:

```text
DRAFT
OPEN
PROCESSING
PROCESSED
PENDING_APPROVAL
APPROVED
LOCKED
PAID
CANCELLED
```

---

# 16. PAYROLL PERIOD RULES

Prevent:

```text
Overlapping payroll periods
Multiple active payroll periods for same scope
Processing locked payroll
Editing paid payroll
```

