# 17. PAYROLL CALCULATION ENGINE

Create a dedicated service:

```text
PayrollCalculationService
```

It should calculate:

```text
Working Days
Calendar Days
Paid Days
Unpaid Days
Leave Days
Absent Days
Present Days
Half Days
Loss of Pay
Overtime
Gross Earnings
Deductions
Employer Contributions
Tax
Net Salary
```

---

# 18. PAYROLL CALCULATION FLOW

Use:

```text
Employee
   ↓
Salary Assignment
   ↓
Payroll Period
   ↓
Working Calendar
   ↓
Attendance
   ↓
Leave
   ↓
Holiday
   ↓
Overtime
   ↓
Earnings
   ↓
Deductions
   ↓
Taxes
   ↓
Net Salary
   ↓
Payroll Result
```

---

# 19. ATTENDANCE INTEGRATION

Use the existing attendance engine.

Payroll must consume:

```text
Present
Absent
Late
Early Exit
Half Day
Weekly Off
Holiday
Work From Home
On Duty
```

Do not recreate attendance calculations inside payroll.

---

# 20. PAID DAYS

Define clearly:

```text
Paid Days
Unpaid Days
LOP Days
```

Example:

```text
Calendar Days = 30
Weekly Off = 8
Holiday = 2
Present = 18
Paid Leave = 1
LOP = 1
```

The exact formula must come from configured payroll policy.

Do not hard-code one universal formula.

---

# 21. LOSS OF PAY

Support configurable LOP calculation.

Example:

```text
Monthly Salary = ₹60,000
Payroll Days = 30
LOP = 2

LOP Deduction =
60,000 / 30 × 2
```

Different tenants may use:

```text
Calendar Days
Working Days
Fixed 30
```

Allow configuration.

---

# 22. HALF-DAY PAYROLL

If an employee has:

```text
Half-day attendance
```

calculate payroll according to policy.

Integrate with Phase 6:

```text
Half-day Leave
+
Half-day Work
```

must not result in double deduction.

---

# 23. LEAVE INTEGRATION

Use Phase 6 leave engine.

Payroll should distinguish:

```text
Paid Leave
Unpaid Leave
Pending Leave
Approved Leave
Rejected Leave
```

Only approved/valid leave should affect payroll according to policy.

Do not directly query raw leave requests without status validation.

---

# 24. HOLIDAY INTEGRATION

Use Phase 6 holiday calendar.

Holiday should normally not cause salary deduction.

But if an employee works on a holiday:

```text
Holiday
+
Attendance
```

provide an extension point for:

```text
Overtime
Holiday Pay
Comp-Off
```

---

# 25. OVERTIME FOUNDATION

If full overtime module is not yet implemented:

Create a payroll-compatible interface:

```text
OvertimeService
```

Example:

```text
approved_overtime_hours
overtime_rate
overtime_amount
```

Payroll should consume approved overtime only.

Do not calculate unauthorized overtime from raw attendance automatically.

---

# 26. EARNINGS ENGINE

Calculate:

```text
Basic
HRA
Allowances
Bonus
Incentive
Commission
Overtime
Reimbursement
Other Earnings
```

Each component must have its own calculation result.

---

# 27. DEDUCTION ENGINE

Calculate:

```text
LOP
Tax
PF
ESI
Professional Tax
Loan
Advance
Other deductions
```

Each deduction must be independently traceable.

---

# 28. COMPONENT CALCULATION

Support:

```text
FIXED
PERCENTAGE_OF_BASIC
PERCENTAGE_OF_GROSS
FORMULA
VARIABLE
```

Example:

```text
HRA = 40% of Basic
```

Do not use unsafe arbitrary Python execution for formulas.

If formula support is implemented, create a controlled expression evaluator.

---

# 29. FORMULA SECURITY

NEVER execute user-provided formulas using:

```text
eval()
exec()
```

Create a safe formula engine.

Allow only approved operations:

```text
+
-
*
/
%
min()
max()
round()
```

and approved variables.

---

# 30. PAYROLL VARIABLES

Potential variables:

```text
BASIC
GROSS
PAID_DAYS
LOP_DAYS
WORKING_DAYS
OVERTIME_HOURS
OVERTIME_AMOUNT
BONUS
INCENTIVE
```

Only expose explicitly approved variables.

---

# 31. ROUNDING

Create configurable rounding rules.

Examples:

```text
Nearest integer
Two decimals
Round half up
Floor
Ceiling
```

Apply rounding consistently.

Do not round intermediate values unnecessarily.

---

# 32. TAX / STATUTORY FOUNDATION

Create configurable architecture for statutory deductions.

Support foundation for:

```text
PF
ESI
Professional Tax
TDS
```

Do not hard-code rates without effective dates/configuration.

For India-specific rules, design the system so rates and thresholds can be updated without code changes.

---

# 33. EFFECTIVE-DATED STATUTORY RULES

Each rule should support:

```text
effective_from
effective_to
region/state
employee applicability
status
```

This is essential because statutory rules change over time.

---

# 34. STATE/REGION CONFIGURATION

Prepare architecture for regional rules such as:

```text
Professional Tax
ESI applicability
Other state-specific deductions
```

Do not assume every employee follows identical rules.

---

# 35. TAX REGIME FOUNDATION

Prepare support for:

```text
Tax Regime
Tax Configuration
Employee Tax Declaration
Taxable Income
Tax Deduction
```

If complete income-tax computation is too large for this phase, implement a clean foundation and clearly mark advanced tax computation for a future phase.

Do not pretend a partial tax engine is production-ready.

---

