```

Do not create another independent approval engine.

---

# 40. PAYROLL APPROVAL

Payroll should support:

```text
Calculate
 ↓
Review
 ↓
Approve
 ↓
Lock
 ↓
Generate Payslips
 ↓
Mark Paid
```

Once locked:

```text
Salary
Attendance input
Leave input
Payroll calculation
```

must not be casually modified.

---

# 41. PAYROLL SNAPSHOT

When payroll is finalized, create an immutable snapshot of calculation inputs/results.

Store:

```text
salary structure version
attendance summary
leave summary
earnings
deductions
tax
contributions
net salary
```

This ensures future employee changes do not alter historical payroll.

---

# 42. HISTORICAL PAYROLL

If an employee's salary changes later:

```text
July payroll
```

must remain unchanged.

Never dynamically recalculate historical paid payroll using current salary configuration.

---

# 43. PAYROLL TRANSACTION MODEL

Use a detailed payroll result.

Example:

```text
Employee:
Neeraj

Basic               40,000
HRA                 20,000
Special Allowance   10,000
Overtime             2,000
--------------------------
Gross               72,000

PF                   4,800
Professional Tax       200
LOP                  1,500
--------------------------
Total Deduction      6,500

Net Salary          65,500
```

Each line item must be independently identifiable.

---

# 44. PAYROLL LINE ITEMS

Create:

```text
PayrollRun
PayrollEmployee
PayrollLineItem
```

or equivalent existing architecture.

Line item types:

```text
EARNING
DEDUCTION
EMPLOYER_CONTRIBUTION
TAX
REIMBURSEMENT
```

---

# 45. NET SALARY

Calculate:

```text
Net Salary =
Total Earnings
-
Employee Deductions
```

Employer contributions must not accidentally reduce employee net salary.

---

# 46. CTC

Calculate separately:

```text
CTC =
Gross
+
Employer Contributions
+
Applicable Benefits
```

Do not mix:

```text
Net Salary
Gross Salary
CTC
```

---

# 47. PAYROLL LOCK

Implement:

```text
LOCKED
```

state.

After locking:

```text
No normal edits
No salary structure changes affecting snapshot
No attendance edits affecting payroll
No leave edits affecting payroll
```

Any correction must use a controlled adjustment/reversal process.

---

# 48. PAYROLL REPROCESSING

Before lock:

```text
Calculate
Recalculate
```

should be allowed.

After lock:

```text
Recalculate
```

should be blocked unless an authorized controlled reopen process exists.

---

# 49. PAYROLL REOPEN

If implemented:

```text
Payroll Admin
   ↓
Reopen Request
   ↓
Approval
   ↓
Unlock
```

Every reopen must be audited.

---

# 50. PAYROLL STATUS MACHINE

Implement a controlled state machine:

```text
DRAFT
 ↓
OPEN
 ↓
PROCESSING
 ↓
PROCESSED
 ↓
PENDING_APPROVAL
 ↓
APPROVED
 ↓
LOCKED
 ↓
PAID
```

Invalid transitions must be rejected.

---

# 51. PAYROLL APPROVAL HISTORY

Record:

```text
actor
action
timestamp
comment
previous_status
new_status
```

Never overwrite approval history.

---

