# 61. PAYROLL EXCEPTIONS

Detect:

```text
Missing salary structure
Missing attendance
Invalid leave
Negative balance
Missing bank/payment information
Invalid statutory configuration
Overlapping salary assignment
Unresolved adjustment
```

Payroll should not silently process invalid data.

---

# 62. EXCEPTION STATES

Use:

```text
WARNING
ERROR
BLOCKING
```

Example:

```text
Missing optional information → WARNING
Missing salary structure → BLOCKING
Invalid payroll configuration → BLOCKING
```

---

# 63. BULK PAYROLL PROCESSING

Support processing many employees efficiently.

Do not perform:

```text
1 database query × every field × every employee
```

Avoid N+1 queries.

Use:

```text
Batch queries
Prefetching
Aggregations
Bulk operations
```

---

# 64. LARGE DATASET TEST

Test with:

```text
10,000 employees
12 months payroll
Multiple salary structures
Large attendance data
Large leave ledger
Large payroll history
```

Measure:

```text
Calculation time
Database queries
Memory
Worker usage
```

---

# 65. BACKGROUND PAYROLL PROCESSING

If Celery exists, use it for heavy payroll processing:

```text
Payroll Calculation
Bulk Payslip Generation
Payroll Reports
Email Distribution
```

The UI should not freeze while calculating thousands of employees.

---

# 66. PAYROLL JOB SAFETY

Background jobs must be:

```text
Idempotent
Retry-safe
Tenant-aware
Auditable
Recoverable
```

A retry must never generate duplicate payroll.

---

# 67. IDEMPOTENCY

Use unique processing identifiers.

Example:

```text
tenant_id
payroll_period_id
employee_id
```

should uniquely identify a payroll employee result for a run.

---

# 68. DATABASE TABLES

Potential tables:

```text
salary_components
salary_structures
salary_structure_components
employee_salary_assignments
payroll_periods
payroll_runs
payroll_employees
payroll_line_items
payroll_adjustments
employee_bonuses
employee_incentives
statutory_rules
tax_configurations
payslips
payroll_approval_records
```

Do not create duplicates if equivalent models already exist.

---

# 69. DATABASE CONSTRAINTS

Use:

```text
Foreign Keys
Unique Constraints
Check Constraints
Tenant Constraints
Effective Date Constraints
Status Constraints
```

Examples:

```text
salary effective_from < effective_to
```

and:

```text
payroll period start_date <= end_date
```

---

# 70. DATABASE INDEXES

Index common queries:

```text
tenant_id
employee_id
payroll_period_id
salary_structure_id
effective_from
effective_to
status
created_at
```

Composite indexes where justified:

```text
tenant_id + employee_id
tenant_id + payroll_period_id
tenant_id + status
tenant_id + effective_from
```

---

# 71. TENANT ISOLATION

Every payroll entity must be tenant-scoped.

Test:

```text
Tenant A cannot see Tenant B payroll.
Tenant A cannot see Tenant B salary.
Tenant A cannot see Tenant B payslips.
Tenant A cannot modify Tenant B payroll.
Tenant A cannot access Tenant B salary structure.
```

