POST   /api/v1/payroll/{id}/calculate
POST   /api/v1/payroll/{id}/process
POST   /api/v1/payroll/{id}/approve
POST   /api/v1/payroll/{id}/lock
POST   /api/v1/payroll/{id}/mark-paid

GET    /api/v1/payroll/{id}/employees
GET    /api/v1/payroll/{id}/employees/{employee_id}

GET    /api/v1/payslips
GET    /api/v1/payslips/{id}
GET    /api/v1/payslips/{id}/download

POST   /api/v1/payroll/adjustments
GET    /api/v1/payroll/adjustments
POST   /api/v1/payroll/adjustments/{id}/approve
```

Use the project's existing API naming conventions if different.

---

# 80. SERVER-SIDE CALCULATION

Never trust frontend values for:

```text
Gross Salary
Net Salary
Tax
Deduction
LOP
Paid Days
Overtime Amount
CTC
```

The backend must calculate and validate all financial values.

---

# 81. FINANCIAL PRECISION

Do NOT use floating-point arithmetic for money.

Use:

```text
Decimal
```

with appropriate PostgreSQL:

```text
NUMERIC
```

precision.

Example:

```text
NUMERIC(14,2)
```

where appropriate.

---

# 82. CURRENCY

Prepare for multi-currency architecture:

```text
currency
currency_code
```

Even if the first release primarily targets INR.

Do not assume every future tenant uses INR.

---

# 83. NEGATIVE VALUES

Define rules for:

```text
Negative salary
Negative deduction
Negative adjustment
Negative balance
```

Do not permit invalid financial values through API manipulation.

---

# 84. PAYROLL RECONCILIATION

Provide reconciliation summary:

```text
Employees processed
Employees skipped
Employees with errors
Gross total
Deduction total
Net total
Employer contribution total
```

Totals must equal line-item aggregates.

---

# 85. PAYROLL VALIDATION

Before lock:

```text
Validate employees
Validate salary
Validate attendance
Validate leave
Validate deductions
Validate statutory rules
Validate calculations
Validate totals
```

If blocking errors exist:

```text
DO NOT LOCK PAYROLL
```

---

# 86. PAYROLL REPORTS

Implement foundation for:

```text
Payroll Summary
Employee Salary Report
Department Salary Report
Branch Salary Report
Earnings Report
Deductions Report
LOP Report
Overtime Report
Tax Report
Employer Contribution Report
```

Support:

```text
CSV
Excel
PDF
```

using the existing reporting architecture.

---

# 87. REPORT FILTERING

Support:

```text
Payroll Period
Employee
Department
Branch
Designation
Salary Structure
Status
```

Use server-side filtering.

---

# 88. EMPLOYEE SELF-SERVICE

Employees should be able to:

```text
View salary
View salary history
View payslips
Download payslips
View payroll summary
```

Employees must never access another employee's salary.

---

# 89. HR SELF-SERVICE

HR/payroll users may:

```text
Manage salary
Assign structures
Process payroll
Review exceptions
Approve payroll
Generate payslips
Run reports
```

subject to RBAC.

---

# 90. FRONTEND ROUTES

Add appropriate pages:

```text
/payroll
/payroll/periods
/payroll/processing
/payroll/review
/payroll/approvals
/payroll/reports
/salary-structures
/salary-components
