Absence
Paid leave
Unpaid leave
Half day
Holiday
Weekly off
LOP
Overtime
Bonus
Incentive
Deduction
```

---

# 103. FINANCIAL CALCULATION TESTS

Verify:

```text
Gross
Deductions
Net
CTC
Employer contributions
Tax
```

Use Decimal and exact expected results.

---

# 104. EDGE CASE TESTS

Test:

```text
Employee joins mid-month
Employee leaves mid-month
Salary changes mid-month
Salary changes mid-year
Leap year
Month with 28 days
Month with 29 days
Month with 30 days
Month with 31 days
Zero attendance
Full absence
Full paid leave
Negative adjustment
Large salary
Large deduction
```

---

# 105. CONCURRENCY TESTS

Test:

```text
Two payroll processes simultaneously
Two approval requests
Duplicate background job
Payroll calculation retry
Payslip generation retry
Salary update during payroll processing
```

---

# 106. TENANT TESTS

Test:

```text
Tenant A payroll isolation
Tenant B payroll isolation
Cross-tenant salary access
Cross-tenant payslip access
Cross-tenant payroll modification
```

---

# 107. RBAC TESTS

Test:

```text
Employee
Manager
HR
Payroll Admin
Tenant Admin
Super Admin
```

Ensure each can perform only authorized actions.

---

# 108. PAYROLL SNAPSHOT TEST

Critical test:

```text
Process payroll
Lock payroll
Change employee salary
Change attendance
Change leave
```

Historical payroll must remain unchanged.

---

# 109. AUDIT TESTS

Verify that:

```text
Salary changes
Payroll approval
Payroll lock
Payroll reopen
Adjustments
Payslip generation
```

all produce appropriate audit records.

---

# 110. PERFORMANCE TESTS

Benchmark:

```text
1,000 employees
5,000 employees
10,000 employees
```

Measure:

```text
Payroll calculation duration
Database queries
Memory
Celery worker performance
Payslip generation time
```

---

# 111. N+1 QUERY PREVENTION

Use query profiling.

Pay particular attention to:

```text
Employee → Salary
Employee → Attendance
Employee → Leave
Payroll → Employee
Payroll → Line Items
```

Avoid loading related data individually.

---

# 112. DATABASE TRANSACTIONS

Payroll finalization must be transactional.

Example:

```text
BEGIN

Validate
Calculate
Create payroll results
Create line items
Create audit
Update status

COMMIT
```

If failure:

```text
ROLLBACK
```

Do not leave partially finalized payroll.

---

# 113. PAYROLL IMMUTABILITY

Once:

```text
PAID
```

historical payroll records should be treated as immutable.

Corrections must use:

```text
Adjustment
Reversal
Next payroll correction
```

rather than directly rewriting history.

---

# 114. DATA RETENTION

Payroll data is financial history.

Do not allow normal CRUD deletion of:

```text
Paid payroll
Payslips
Payroll line items
Approval history
Payroll audit
```

---

# 115. ERROR HANDLING

Create stable error codes:

```text
SALARY_STRUCTURE_NOT_FOUND
SALARY_ASSIGNMENT_INVALID
SALARY_OVERLAP
PAYROLL_PERIOD_OVERLAP
PAYROLL_ALREADY_LOCKED
PAYROLL_ALREADY_PAID
PAYROLL_CALCULATION_FAILED
PAYROLL_VALIDATION_FAILED
MISSING_SALARY_STRUCTURE
MISSING_ATTENDANCE
INVALID_PAYROLL_STATE
PAYROLL_APPROVAL_REQUIRED
PAYROLL_ACCESS_DENIED
PAYSLIP_ACCESS_DENIED
INVALID_FINANCIAL_VALUE
```

---

# 116. API PAGINATION

Paginate:

```text
Payroll Employees
Payroll History
Payslips
Salary History
Payroll Adjustments
Payroll Reports
```

Do not return unlimited records.

---

# 117. SEARCH

Support server-side:

```text
Employee Name
Employee ID
Department
Branch
Payroll Period
Status
```

