# 127. CRITICAL DEVELOPMENT PRINCIPLE

Do NOT build Phase 7 as a simple CRUD application.

Payroll is a **financial calculation engine**.

The implementation must correctly handle:

```text
Salary history
Effective dates
Attendance
Leave
Holidays
Working days
LOP
Earnings
Deductions
Overtime
Bonus
Incentives
Taxes
Employer contributions
Net salary
CTC
Payroll approval
Payroll locking
Historical snapshots
Financial precision
Concurrency
Audit
Tenant isolation
Security
```

---

# FINAL INSTRUCTION TO THE AI CODING AGENT

Inspect the existing AxonTimeHR repository completely before modifying it.

Do not rewrite working Phase 1–6 functionality.

Do not create duplicate:

```text
Employee
Attendance
Shift
Leave
Holiday
Approval
Authentication
RBAC
Tenant
Audit
Notification
```

systems.

Reuse existing services and models.

Implement Phase 7 incrementally:

```text
1. Repository analysis
2. Payroll architecture
3. Salary component master
4. Salary structure
5. Employee salary assignment
6. Salary versioning
7. Payroll periods
8. Payroll calculation engine
9. Attendance integration
10. Leave integration
11. Holiday integration
12. Earnings engine
13. Deduction engine
14. LOP
15. Overtime foundation
16. Bonus
17. Incentive
18. Adjustments
19. Statutory foundation
20. Payroll approval
21. Payroll locking
22. Payroll snapshot
23. Payslip generation
24. Reports
25. Employee self-service
26. Notifications
27. Background processing
28. Security
29. Audit
30. Testing
31. Performance optimization
32. Regression testing
33. Documentation
```

After every major component:

```text
Implement
   ↓
Run tests
   ↓
Fix failures
   ↓
Validate database
   ↓
Validate financial calculations
   ↓
Validate security
   ↓
Validate tenant isolation
   ↓
Run regression
   ↓
Continue
```

The final implementation must be:

**production-ready, financially accurate, multi-tenant, secure, auditable, scalable, configurable, workflow-driven, and extensible.**

Most importantly:

**Never modify historical paid payroll directly. Preserve financial history through immutable payroll snapshots, ledger-style records, approvals, adjustments, and audit trails.**

Design the payroll engine so future AxonTimeHR modules such as **Overtime, Comp-Off, Expenses, Loans, Advances, Tax Filing, Accounting and Bank Payment Integration** can plug into it without requiring a major rewrite.
